 },
 "description": "RS256 assertion and token-exchange vectors (--direction token). lm15 pins ONE JWT serialization: header and payload as compact JSON (no spaces) with keys in the order shown, base64url without padding, RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5/SHA-256 over '<header>.<payload>'. The servers accept any valid JSON (RFC 7519); the pinned order is lm15's canonical fact so that four ports produce identical bytes. Every value here is fake: the key is the corpus test key, the tenant/client/project ids are placeholders, the response tokens are plain marker strings. 'now' is the fixed clock the shim must use. A value of the form {\"$file\": <repo path>, \"strip_comment_lines\"?: true} is expanded by the HARNESS to that file's contents (dropping lines that start with '#' when asked) before the op is sent; the shim never reads the repository.",
